{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/174195-supernatural-merits-and-cover","id":174195,"title":"Supernatural Merits and Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-19T09:29:59-07:00","id":174195,"title":"Supernatural Merits and Cover","content":"Just a quick question but can demon covers have supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:16:00-07:00","id":174259,"title":"","content":"Technically? No. A character with Supernatural Tolerance can't buy Supernatural Merits, and a human with Supernatural Merits who becomes a supernatural creature in play loses those Merits and reallocates the points per the Sanctity of Merits (GMC p. 172).<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, Supernatural Merits pack far less wallop for the Experiences than do Embeds or Exploits, so the danger of abuse is usually pretty low. In my WoD, if you want to spend XP on Pyrokinesis for some character/story reason instead of buying, I dunno, Hellfire, I'm probably going to be okay with that.<br /> <br /> As well, if you make a pact with a powerful telekinetic (or whatever) during the course of play, that's cool by me. However, I don't want to see a character with three different Covers, all of which possess an insane number of Supernatural Merits in order to allow you to be a Swiss army knife of cool supernatural abilities, especially if two of them are Covers you bought at character generation.<br /> <br /> Regarding using Legend to &quot;pretend&quot; to be a mage/vampire/werewolf by mimicking some of their abilities as Supernatural Merits, it doesn't work like that. A demon who gains the Cover of a supernatural being only gets the &quot;human half&quot; of that creature, so the demon can't then use Legend to mimic those powers in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:29:41-07:00","id":174366,"title":"","content":"Cools thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T01:12:41-07:00","id":175859,"title":"","content":"There is a work around, presuming your ST is willing.<br /> <br /> In Reliquary, there's a type of relic that has it's own merits, including unseen senses, so the case can be made that relics with other supernatural merits should be available: glasses of telepathy, rings of psychokinesis.<br /> <br /> One might even want to make relic creator a supernatural merit so that there are relic creating stigmatics in their game. <br /> <br /> Although I imagine the argument could be made that unless one is wearing an occultist type cover that having a collection of mystical artifacts is probably cover damaging. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}